{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>For</b> — These are the words of the prophet, reproving Israel and comforting them: if the House is destroyed, we will not forsake the Torah of our Elohim, who promised us and made us hear such things. Or the meaning is Israel's departure from exile; therefore the word: <b>and we will walk</b>, and this is the meaning — for when the House is built, then the nations will bring Israel, the scattered ones, as an offering to YHWH, and in their going each man will walk <b>in the name of his god</b>, until the people of the Temple instruct them; therefore what follows it."], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "Resolved ה' in 'מנחה לה׳' as YHWH per divine-name conventions. The phrase עד שיורום אנשי בית המקדש is rendered hyper-literally; the syntax is compressed and the referent of the instruction is ambiguous."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:13:52.791947759Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}